 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S443-017\", \"clauses\": {\"recognize_and_represent\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"Use base-10 blocks to show the number {total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F18 asks the learner to represent a generated total with base-10 blocks, which is the recognize-and-represent task. Its total is drawn from the generated number, with printed values from 203 to 987.\"}, \"numbers\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"Use base-10 blocks to show the number {total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F18 prints a numeral total, so the object of the competency (numbers) is what the problem addresses.\"}, \"up_to_1000\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"Use base-10 blocks to show the number {total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"The declared bound is 10 to 1000 and F18 prints totals across that range, with observed values up to 987, so problems span the range the competency names.\"}, \"concrete_models\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"Use base-10 blocks to show the number {total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"Base-10 blocks are the concrete model. F18 requires the learner to show the number with them.\"}, \"pictorial_models\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F15\", \"template\": \"Move the dot to show {value}{suffix}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F15 places a value on a number line, a pictorial model. Its suffix is the gated word 'number line', and its values are drawn from the generated number with observed values up to 971.\"}, \"numerals\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F18\", \"template\": \"Use base-10 blocks to show the number {total}.\", \"reasoning\": \"F18 presents the target as a numeral, so the learner works with numerals in the problem text.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F07\", \"F08\", \"F10\", \"F11\", \"F12\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Multiply each block's own value by how many there are, then add all the totals together.\", \"{capitalize}: {digit} block{v}.\", \"{chunk}-{v}\", \"{p0} {p1}\", \"{v} hundred\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F07 is a hint whose template prints the verb Multiply. That teaches multiplication, which is NOT_YET_KNOWN for this lc, and template_chosen_by_values lists task_type, so the template is reachable. F08 has two defects. Its capitalize slot draws from a list that includes Hundreds, which is a NOT_YET_KNOWN word. Its v slot is a separate domain from digit, with members empty and s, and nothing ties it to digit, so the plural can disagree with the count (for example a count of 1 with the plural suffix, or a count of 2 with no suffix). F10 draws chunk from the tens list and v from the ones list, and both lists include the empty string, so the domain can print a dangling hyphen, a bare ones word, or a tens word with no ones word. Both are malformed answer choices, and a tens word joined to a teen word is not a number name. F11 joins p0, which is a F12 phrase, with p1 from the ones list, which includes the empty string. This can print a leading space, a bare hundred phrase, or a hundred phrase followed by a teen word, which names a number above 1000. F12 prints v followed by the word hundred with v from the ones list including the empty string, so it can print a bare hundred phrase, or a phrase for 1100 to 1900 that is outside the 10 to 1000 bound. F09, F14 and F18 are correct as far as the declared domains show, and the clauses are producible from F18 and F15. The distractor families F10, F11 and F12 are the ones whose text cannot be read as numbers for a learner of this grade and quarter.\"}",
